{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "urn:ergo:eip-0045:b4-negative-verifier-input-v1",
  "title": "Eip0045B4NegativeVerifierInputV1",
  "$comment": "The fixed subject and positional context prefix make role/path uniqueness, order, and the component-prefix antichain schema-complete for every schema-valid V1 instance. The matching parser additionally rechecks the antichain as defense in depth. Exact per-dispatch context cardinalities remain a fail-closed handler-freeze gate: schema validity alone does not make an input campaign-precommit eligible.",
  "description": "One implementation-neutral B4 negative verifier input containing only one of the 20 canonical dispatch pairs and exact positional physical identities. It contains no execution, QA, expectation, implementation, descriptor, or attribution field.",
